# 4️⃣ Find Largest Element That Appears More Than Once

### Array

```java
int[] arr = {4, 7, 2, 7, 9, 4, 7};
```

Expected answer:

```text
Largest Duplicate = 7
```

### Code

```java
int[] arr = {4, 7, 2, 7, 9, 4, 7};

int largest = Integer.MIN_VALUE;

for(int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {

    int count = 0;

    for(int j = 0; j < arr.length; j++) {
        if(arr[i] == arr[j]) {
            count++;
        }
    }

    if(count >= 2 && arr[i] > largest) {
        largest = arr[i];
    }
}

System.out.println("Largest Duplicate = " + largest);
```

### Output

```text
Largest Duplicate = 7
```

### 🧠 Important

Two conditions are required:

```java
count >= 2
```

→ element is duplicated

```java
arr[i] > largest
```

→ find the largest duplicate

### Complexity

- Time: `O(n²)`
- Space: `O(1)`

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

# 5️⃣ Find Smallest Duplicate Element

### Array

```java
int[] arr = {5, 3, 8, 3, 2, 5, 8, 8};
```

Expected:

```text
Smallest Duplicate = 3
```

### Code

```java
int[] arr = {5, 3, 8, 3, 2, 5, 8, 8};

int smallest = Integer.MAX_VALUE;

for(int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {

    int count = 0;

    for(int j = 0; j < arr.length; j++) {
        if(arr[i] == arr[j]) {
            count++;
        }
    }

    if(count >= 2 && arr[i] < smallest) {
        smallest = arr[i];
    }
}

System.out.println("Smallest Duplicate = " + smallest);
```

### Output

```text
Smallest Duplicate = 3
```

### 🧠 Largest vs Smallest

```text
Largest:
Integer.MIN_VALUE
arr[i] > largest

Smallest:
Integer.MAX_VALUE
arr[i] < smallest
```

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

# 6️⃣ Find Frequency of the Largest Element

### Array

```java
int[] arr = {4, 7, 2, 7, 9, 4, 7};
```

Expected:

```text
Largest = 9
Frequency = 1
```

### Code

```java
int[] arr = {4, 7, 2, 7, 9, 4, 7};

int largest = Integer.MIN_VALUE;

for(int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
    if(arr[i] > largest) {
        largest = arr[i];
    }
}

int count = 0;

for(int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
    if(arr[i] == largest) {
        count++;
    }
}

System.out.println("Largest = " + largest);
System.out.println("Frequency = " + count);
```

### Complexity

- Time: `O(n)`
- Space: `O(1)`

### 💡 Pattern

This is a **two-pass approach**:

```text
Pass 1 → Find largest
Pass 2 → Count largest
```

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

