# 🔟 Find the Most Frequent Element

### Array

```java
int[] arr = {2, 5, 2, 8, 5, 2, 8};
```

Expected:

```text
Most Frequent = 2
Max Frequency = 3
```

### Code

```java
int[] arr = {2, 5, 2, 8, 5, 2, 8};

int maxFrequency = 0;
int mostFrequent = 0;

for(int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {

    int count = 0;

    for(int j = 0; j < arr.length; j++) {

        if(arr[i] == arr[j]) {
            count++;
        }
    }

    if(count > maxFrequency) {
        maxFrequency = count;
        mostFrequent = arr[i];
    }
}

System.out.println("Most Frequent = " + mostFrequent);
System.out.println("Max Frequency = " + maxFrequency);
```

### Output

```text
Most Frequent = 2
Max Frequency = 3
```

### 🧠 Variable Meaning

This was one of the most important concepts from today's practice:

```text
count
↓
Frequency of the CURRENT element

maxFrequency
↓
Highest frequency found so far

mostFrequent
↓
Element having the highest frequency
```

### Complexity

- Time: `O(n²)`
- Space: `O(1)`

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

# 🧠 MOST IMPORTANT PATTERNS FROM DAY 6

## 1. Counting Pattern

```java
int count = 0;

for(...) {
    if(condition) {
        count++;
    }
}
```

Use when the question asks:

- How many?
- Count occurrences
- Count even/odd
- Count positive/negative

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

## 2. Largest Pattern

```java
int largest = Integer.MIN_VALUE;

if(arr[i] > largest) {
    largest = arr[i];
}
```

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

## 3. Smallest Pattern

```java
int smallest = Integer.MAX_VALUE;

if(arr[i] < smallest) {
    smallest = arr[i];
}
```

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

## 4. Frequency Pattern

```java
for(int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {

    int count = 0;

    for(int j = 0; j < arr.length; j++) {

        if(arr[i] == arr[j]) {
            count++;
        }
    }
}
```

### Memory trick:

**Outer loop = WHICH element?**

**Inner loop = HOW MANY?**

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

## 5. Duplicate Pattern

```java
if(count >= 2)
```

Means:

> The element appears at least twice.

`count > 1` is also equivalent.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

## 6. Unique Pattern

```java
if(count == 1)
```

Means:

> The element appears exactly once.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

# ⚠️ Common Mistakes to Avoid

### Mistake 1 — Not resetting count

❌ Wrong:

```java
int count = 0;

for(int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
    ...
}
```

when counting each element separately.

✅ Correct:

```java
for(int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
    int count = 0;
    ...
}
```

### Mistake 2 — Comparing the wrong variables

For most frequent:

❌ Wrong:

```java
if(mostFrequent > maxFrequency)
```

✅ Correct:

```java
if(count > maxFrequency)
```

Because:

```text
count = frequency
maxFrequency = frequency
```

### Mistake 3 — Updating only one variable

For most frequent:

```java
if(count > maxFrequency) {
    maxFrequency = count;
    mostFrequent = arr[i];
}
```

Both must be updated.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

# 🎯 Interview Tips

When you see words like:

| Question says | Think |
|---|---|
| Frequency | Count occurrences |
| Duplicate | `count >= 2` |
| Unique | `count == 1` |
| Most frequent | Maximum frequency |
| Least frequent | Minimum frequency |
| Largest duplicate | Duplicate + maximum |
| Smallest duplicate | Duplicate + minimum |
| Largest unique | Unique + maximum |
| Smallest unique | Unique + minimum |

### ⭐ Very important distinction

```text
i
```

means **index**

```text
arr[i]
```

means **value**

Example:

```java
arr[i] > largest
```

You are comparing the **value**.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

